{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-cli/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:00:08.328768Z","id":"45655bf9e9144eb20d1140747fd8adad2b1d6edb78a2fb6fc301ed86593abf8b","body":{"detail":"//crates/clax-cli:clax_android_arm64 is 34.95 MB stripped (.text 22.8 MB) where scripts/build-app-clax.sh android's cargo --release build of the same source was 28.18 MB (.text 18.7 MB), and x86_64 39.3 MB against 31.0 MB (llvm-size -A, 2026-10-17). Both are dynamically linked against libc.so, libm.so and libdl.so only. Likely causes, not confirmed: crate_universe gives each third-party crate the workspace's merged features (docs/bazel.md, Differences from Cargo), so test-only features of tokio and others reach the binary, and workspace crates keep line tables until the final strip. The APK grows by about 6 MB compressed.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":65},"content_hash":"d2bf40027b27ae6925c48c22e75597974839384630749a5e787ee1f9969e61af"},"suggested_fix":"Compare cargo tree -e features -p clax-cli --target aarch64-linux-android with the features in bazel/workspace.bzl, and if dev features are the cause, give the Android build a crate_universe annotation or a separate crates repository without them.","summary":"Bazel's Android clax is about a quarter larger than Cargo's","tags":["android","size","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
